// Ore on the map (WP7.1): amounts per cell, taking, depletion and slow regrowth on the
// 256 by 256 cell playfield (assets/maps/playfield256, 215 ore cells in eight fields).
// Pinned by ore_256.expected; the test tools/sf_headless/tests/ore.rs asserts the amounts.
// The ore rules are written out here (a frozen copy of the idea of assets/config/ore.ron, with
// a short regrowth period so that 600 ticks show it): editing the shipped file never moves
// this checksum.
//
//   field A  28 cells around (118, 82): emptied at tick 5 (take 500 from every cell)
//   field B  27 cells around (46, 118): 80 taken from every cell at tick 5 (40 left)
//   field C  47 cells around (53, 234): untouched
//   (the other five fields are untouched too)
//
// A cell grows by 2 every 20 ticks, in the ticks t with t % 20 == its place in the list of the
// 215 ore cells (row-major) % 20, up to 160. There are no entities.
Scenario(
    name: "ore_256",
    seed: 0x0E57_0071,
    map: (width: 256, height: 256),
    map_name: Some("playfield256"),
    ore: Some((start: 120, max: 160, regrow_amount: 2, regrow_period: 20)),
    ticks: 600,
    commands: [
        (tick: 5, command: TakeOre(cell: (118, 79), amount: 500)),
        (tick: 5, command: TakeOre(cell: (116, 80), amount: 500)),
        (tick: 5, command: TakeOre(cell: (117, 80), amount: 500)),
        (tick: 5, command: TakeOre(cell: (118, 80), amount: 500)),
